{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/829255-questions-on-infrastructure-help","id":829255,"title":"Questions on Infrastructure (Help!)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-13T08:22:06-08:00","id":829255,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Questions on Infrastructure (Help!)","content":"I keep getting caught in a loop with Infrastructure, where I imagine it like the buildings you'd see in a real-time strategy game, like Warcraft or Red Alert, with a tech-tree and everything. The problem is I'm not sure on whether that's grossly inaccurate, considering Infrastructure can range between said-buildings to things like vaccum-cleaners and various paraphernalia. I mean, if that's the case, does that mean Infrastructure can equate to a gadget?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T08:43:56-08:00","id":829264,"title":"","content":"Infrastructure is a case where your roleplayer's instincts betray you. As White Wolf/Onyx Path fans, we're used to coming upon words not common in everyday language, used in association with some kind of supernatural thing, and thinking of them as Proper Nouns, names for a specific game concept that only relate to their normal definition loosely or metaphorically. With infrastructure, this is not the case. <i>The God-Machine's infrastructure literally is anything that would serve as infrastructure, in the normal sense, for the God-Machine.</i> Infrastructure, in this case, literally just means &quot;a material thing or things the God-Machine is using to accomplish a task.&quot;<br /> <br /> Are there people being used as a workforce, knowingly or not, to align whatever magical confluence the God-Machine needs to happen? Those people are infrastructure. Is there an office they work in that supports their magical task? That office is infrastructure. Do they work on special materials that have to be imported from deep beneath the earth's crust using a supernatural high-speed elevator? The elevator is infrastructure. Does the God-Machine regulate their work with subliminal messaging hidden in the smooth jazz that plays over the office intercom? The intercom is infrastructure.<br /> <br /> Being used as infrastructure doesn't automatically make something magical. Those people can just be normal human beings. That office might just be an ordinary office. Some infrastructure is magical, though, especially if it's supported by other infrastructure. That elevator is probably supernatural in some way, and probably has some kind of glaringly weird linchpin, like oversized hearts pumping inside the circuit breakers maybe. The use of infrastructure also can support supernatural phenomena: specifically, angels use the presence of an active project to manifest the same way ghosts use anchors and spirits use resonance. But the quality of infrastructure isn't intrinsic to an object. It's a consequence of what the object is doing, what purpose it is being used for.<br /> <br /> Infrastructure with supernatural effects, like the high speed elevator and its supernatural underground ores, are often imbued with them through occult matrices caused by other projects. The God-Machine's projects are linked together in huge, complicated support networks, so that disrupting one project might set many others back as well.<br /> <br /> The vocabulary, put simply:<br /> <br /> <b>Infrastructure:</b> People, places or things the God-Machine is using to achieve an output.<br /> <b>Output:</b> A supernatural result or goal the God-Machine wants to cause.<br /> <b>Occult matrix:</b> A sort of ritual or rare confluence of events that, when lined up correctly, causes a given output.<br /> <b>Project:</b> The planning and work that goes into lining up an occult matrix. The verb to infrastructure's noun.<br /> <b>Linchpin:</b> A failure point in a project. A means of disrupting the occult matrix or preventing the God-Machine from using the infrastructure.<br /> <b>Facility:</b> A location so closely plugged into the God-Machine's workings that it's effectively a direct part of the God-Machine. Often these locations are extradimensional folded spaces, like a demon's bolthole writ large. Nearly everything in a facility is probably infrastructure being put to some kind of use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T08:48:15-08:00","id":829267,"title":"","content":"Shit. That complicates what I was planning then. Back to the drawing-board.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T09:26:26-08:00","id":829277,"title":"","content":"What were you planning? Could be some way to make something similar work, even if it's not quite the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T10:44:22-08:00","id":829312,"title":"","content":"I pictured infrastructure like setting up a base on a map. CCs being at the &quot;center&quot;, and the rest being akin to Towers, Barracks, etc. Of course, the other idea was Infrastructure was another way of saying &quot;shrine&quot; which could upgrade itself to Temple, to Chapel, or something-something. With the linchpin being maybe the altar or similar. Yeah, my thoughts are all over the place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 02-13-2016, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T11:37:31-08:00","id":829341,"title":"","content":"That's in the game in the form of Facilities. Might try to elaborate if I can get back to my books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T15:06:01-08:00","id":829425,"title":"","content":"Fair deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Wa